# t6-avif-encode: integration fragment

## native/core/Cargo.lock, native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml (lead regenerates)

mixdog-imaging gains one dependency: `ravif = { version = "=0.12.0", default-features = false }` (already written in
crates/mixdog-imaging/Cargo.toml). It pulls in rav1e 0.8.1, avif-serialize 0.8.8, imgref, loop9, quick-error, v_frame,
av1-grain, av-scenechange 0.14.1 and their dependencies, all of which are in the local cargo registry cache; the build
needs `cargo ... --offline` without `--locked` once so the lock gains them, and the workspace-hack regenerates for the
unified features. `asm` (nasm) and `threading` of ravif/rav1e are off: the encoder runs on one thread, as the encoder
of libheif does for one picture.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose.rs, native_ext_methods

When the whole image corpus passes with AVIF outputs really AVIF (mixdog-imaging node_twin, avif_reference,
still_twin and mixdog-exthost-worker methods_twin), the filter `.filter(|method| !method.starts_with("image."))` that
keeps image.* on the script worker is removed, so the Rust worker answers image.probe, image.jpeg, image.validate,
image.resize and image.still.

## SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs)

No protocol method is added or registered by this task: nothing to remove from SERVICE_PENDING.
